    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA McGee are delighted to present No. 74A Coolamber Drive to the market.\r\n\r\nThis beautiful 4 bedroom semi-detatched home extends to approximately 124 sq. m. offering well-proportioned accommodation throughout and presents an excellent opportunity for buyers looking to acquire a family home with excellent potential.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are welcomed by a spacious entrance hall which leads through to a generous living room/dining area, providing a comfortable space for relaxing and family living. To the rear of the property is the kitchen which overlooks the beautiful south-east facing rear garden. Further through the kitchen we enter into the attached garage space which benefits from a guest w/c. Upstairs, the property comprises two large double bedrooms, two spacious single bedrooms and a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nExternally, No. 74A benefits from a fully enclosed south-east facing rear garden, offering a private outdoor space and side access. The property also benefits from off-street parking to the front. The property has also recently benefited from wrap-around external insulation, enhancing its thermal efficiency and contributing to improved warmth and comfort throughout the property.\r\n\r\nCoolamber is a mature and established residential development situated in Rathcoole, offering residents a convenient and family-friendly setting. Rathcoole itself provides a range of local amenities, including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and community services. The location is particularly attractive for commuters, with excellent access to the N7 and M50 motorway networks, providing convenient connectivity to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The area is also well served by public transport, with regular bus services providing access to Dublin and other surrounding locations. The nearby Citywest Business Campus and Citywest Shopping Centre further enhance the convenience of the location."
      },
